# ue-vscode-helper

Dual-host Unreal IntelliSense extension: **Cursor** (clangd + slim BuildRules C#) vs **VS Code** (Microsoft C++).

## Hard rules (never regress)

- **C++ (Cursor):** `clangd.enable: true`; `C_Cpp.intelliSenseEngine` (and autocomplete/squiggles/formatting) **disabled**. Root `compile_commands.json`. `.clangd`: project Source keeps real diagnostics — **NEVER** project-wide `Suppress: ["*"]`. Engine PathMatch only: `Suppress: ["*"]` + `Index.Background: Skip`.
- **C# (Cursor):** Write `.vscode/<Project>.BuildRules.IntelliSense.csproj` (UBT + EpicGames.Build only, **no UE5Rules**) **and** sibling `.sln`. Set `dotnet.defaultSolution` to the **`.sln` path** — never bare `.csproj`, never root `*.sln`, never Intermediate ModuleRules. Bare csproj is ignored → root ModuleRules→UE5Rules (~2500 files) hangs / “Miscellaneous Files”.
- **Setup UX:** Write settings before restore; restore slim csproj with 90s timeout (non-fatal); Reload Window prompt **outside** `withProgress`. Re-run Setup after Unreal “Generate VS Code project files”.
- **Host:** `resolveHost()` via `preferHost` or `/cursor/i` on `appName`.

## Layout

`src/host.ts`, `engine.ts`, `excludes.ts`, `profiles/cursor.ts`, `profiles/vscode.ts`, `extension.ts`, `git.ts`.

Full knowledge base: `.cursor/skills/ue-helper/SKILL.md`.
